From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GTK][WPE] Let Rockchip's MPP video decoder into the sandbox

On Rockchip SoCs, GStreamer reaches the hardware video decoder through
Rockchip's Media Process Platform (MPP), which opens /dev/mpp_service,
allocates from /dev/dma_heap and reads the device tree to identify the
SoC. The sandbox has none of them, so the web process finds no hardware
decoder and plays video in software, while the same pipeline outside
the sandbox decodes in hardware. Bind them like the vendor GPU nodes
already bound: each is skipped where it does not exist.

The paths must be device binds: a plain bind is mounted nodev, and
opening /dev/mpp_service through one fails with EACCES.

* Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp:
(WebKit::bindRockchipMPP):
(WebKit::bubblewrapSpawn):

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/BubblewrapLauncher.cpp
@@ -518,6 +518,17 @@
     }
 }
 
+static void bindRockchipMPP(Vector<CString>& args)
+{
+    // Rockchip's Media Process Platform: its codec service, the DMA heaps it allocates from,
+    // and the device tree it identifies the SoC by.
+    args.appendList({
+        "--dev-bind-try", "/dev/mpp_service", "/dev/mpp_service",
+        "--dev-bind-try", "/dev/dma_heap", "/dev/dma_heap",
+        "--ro-bind-try", "/sys/firmware/devicetree", "/sys/firmware/devicetree",
+    });
+}
+
 static bool enableDebugPermissions()
 {
     static int enabled = -1;
@@ -957,6 +968,7 @@
 
         // Although cameras can be managed via the DesktopPortal, we still need v4l2 for video decoding.
         bindV4l(sandboxArgs);
+        bindRockchipMPP(sandboxArgs);
 
 #if USE(ATSPI)
         auto accessibilityBusAddress = launchOptions.extraInitializationData.get("accessibilityBusAddress"_s);
